Symptom: searching for customers named "O'Brien" returns HTTP 500 with "syntax error at or near Brien". Every other name works.
Reproduce: GET /customers?name=O'Brien. Observed in production. Changed recently: nothing in this file for months.

```js
app.get('/customers', async (req, res) => {
  const rows = await db.query("SELECT * FROM customers WHERE name = '" + req.query.name + "'")
  res.json(rows)
})
```

Symptom: the counter on the dashboard shows 1 forever, even though the interval fires every second (a console.log inside it prints).
Reproduce: open /dashboard, wait 5 seconds. Observed locally and in staging. Changed recently: moved from a class component to hooks.

```jsx
function Ticker() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0)
  useEffect(() => {
    const id = setInterval(() => setCount(count + 1), 1000)
    return () => clearInterval(id)
  }, [])
  return <span>{count}</span>
}
```

